A||||8||Shiner||KYB vs. Monroe Sensatrack||||1||
Z||000000||Shiner||10-30-2000||09:58 PM||||Well, the beast is going to need shocks and struts once I get it back on the road, and Monroe is having a buy 3 get one free sale.  Now, what do you guys think of the Monroes?  I really want a harder, better performing shock, not one that rides like my grandpa's caddy.  Are they too soft?  And what are they like compared to the KYBs?  Do they perform better or worse?<P> Thanks in advance!<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000001||WisconsinGT||10-30-2000||11:58 PM||||Shiner, I have Monroe Sensatrack's on my 88GT. I have never used or experienced KYB's. But I can tell you that if you plan on doing any autocrossing you might want to go with KYB's. Otherwise, Monroes are great!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||10-31-2000||01:54 AM||||Had Monroe's initially. I have KYB's now. The KYB's are slightly stiffer but not too stiff. KYB's are sort of in between Monroe's and Koni's. I have heard Gabrielle's (sp?) are about the same as Monroe's. Monroe's are slightly better than stock. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||10-31-2000||07:47 AM||||I've got the KYBs on my Formula, and I am very pleased with them. I don't know anything about the others.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric_PA||10-31-2000||09:43 AM||||<BR>Hey Shiner, this has nothing to do with the shock question, but I have to redo mine soon also. I head through your way everyday after work and once in a while I pass a white GT fastback on 412. Could that be you? just wondering. I am usually driving my Black Sunfire GT and sometimes in my Fiero.<P>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 GT<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||Shiner||10-31-2000||02:42 PM||||Thanks for the input guys, looks like I'll stick it out for the KYB's.<P>Eric,<BR> Nope, that's not me.  My GT is gold (soon to be orange or red), the parts car is red, and they are both at my father's house in Perkasie.  I still have the '84 parked at my place, but we are pretty much on 611, not 412.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||04:32 PM||||I have KYB shocks on my 88. Anyone have the struts on there 88. I heard that they have to be modified to fit on 88's is this true?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000007||88formula||10-31-2000||05:04 PM||||I didn't have to modify the rear struts when I installed them on my formula.||||reg||1
Z||000008||TheFiero64||11-01-2000||10:21 AM||||That's good. I heard that on one of the lists a wile back. Thanks 88formula<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
